{"dog":{"age_group":"young","application_url":"https://www.nycacc.org/adopt/adoption-process/","availability_detail":"available","breed_display":"Domestic Short Hair Cross","breed_primary":"Domestic Short Hair Cross","description_text":"My foster writes: Eucalyptus is a little ball of energy! He never met a feather wand, ribbon, or ball he didn't want to chase, and treats are his love language. He started out shy, but a little playtime and a few snacks won him over - now he follows his people from room to room angling for pets, and he's not afraid to chirp and ask for them.\n\nFiesta is the calmer half. He's happy to settle in next to you on the couch, though he likes space on his own terms, and he saves his playful side for games with Eucalyptus. Once having a couple weeks to warm up, he has settled into being the steady, easygoing one of the pair.\n\nMy foster writes:\nEucalyptus is an energetic ball of fun who loves to chat, while Fiesta is his calm, shy shadow who prefers to stay out of trouble and observe from a cozy hiding spot. Eucalyptus is always ready for action and will happily chase strings and long feather toys, or independently bat around springs and fuzz balls. While neither are big fans of cuddling or being petted just yet, they can both be tempted and won over with a tasty treat like a Churu.","detail_url":"https://nycaccpets.shelterbuddy.com/animal/animalDetails.asp?s=adoption&searchTypeId=4&animalType=2%2C15&pagesize=75&task=view&tpage=8&searchType=4&animalid=203276","id":"8e430b549273489aa4f259d91683e3e8","image_urls":["https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/a89d2d19f3524fc9bf6530ecf71d050f-1789998113-1790013886-png/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/e95bb30600d046468699b5603efb1083-1790013825-1790013825-png/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/b7d4af47336a4746a1437b3c2db85b78-1789998114-1789998114-png/600---n","https://nycacc.shelterbuddy.com/storage/image/f6c8e9cda12c44fb81107194f0186143-1789998100